{
  "id": "edition-revision-reanchor",
  "kind": "reanchor",
  "description": "Anchors carried from one content revision to the next, in the order specs/03 fixes: stable token ids, then the id_lineage revision mapping, then the exact quote with its context, else orphaned. Three pairs: Genesis 1:1 (WLC) re-segmented into morphemes with the text unchanged, so a note on a split word keeps its range through the lineage; John 3:16 (BSB) edited so that one 'that' and 'one and' are deleted, where stable ids carry later notes across the shift, a lineage deletion orphans a note instead of letting its quote land on the later 'that', and a note on deleted words is orphaned; and a study note with pointed Hebrew, an emoji with a skin-tone modifier and bidi isolates, re-anchored by quote alone across an edit, with the expected UTF-16 range alongside the scalar range, and a variant where the quote recurs so the result is ambiguous. Expected offsets were computed in Python independently of the Rust implementation.",
  "license": "WLC text: public domain; OSHB markup CC BY 4.0. BSB: public domain. Note text: CC0, written for this fixture. The edited John 3:16 and the next WLC revision are hypothetical.",
  "source": "Genesis 1:1 as in hebrew-cantillation-genesis-1; John 3:16 as in cross-verse-selection-john-3; note text written for this fixture.",
